WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:02.735
-You know, before the show,
Jamie and I were talking about

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.637
some of our favorite '90s
R&amp;B groups.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.806
And we got reminiscing
about this duo

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.575
that we both loved,
named Take Two.

00:00:09.575 --> 00:00:12.411
If you don't remember Take Two,
they were this an R&amp;B duo

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:14.981
who were famous
for doing the flirty dialogue

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.983
at the beginning of R&amp;B songs.

00:00:16.983 --> 00:00:18.117
But here's the thing --

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:20.086
they never actually
got to the singing part.

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.521
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.521 --> 00:00:23.222
They only did the talking
at the start.

00:00:23.222 --> 00:00:25.892
Well, I just found this
old commercial for their music.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:27.293
Check this out.
[ Applause ]

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:30.963
-The R&amp;B box set you've been
waiting for is finally here.

00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.932
It's "The Complete Take Two."

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.500
This special collector's edition

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.502
includes all
your Take Two favorites,

00:00:36.502 --> 00:00:39.539
like their number-two
smash hit, "Hey Girl."

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:42.542
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:50.583 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:53.052
-Hey, girl.

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:54.754
-It's been a long time.

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:58.124
-But lately,
you've been on my mind.

00:00:58.124 --> 00:01:00.159 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:04.430
-So, tonight, I wanted
to tell you how special you are.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:09.702
-That's right. And it goes
a little something like --

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.772
Well, there's actually
are a couple of things

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.173
I want to tell you.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:16.308
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.308 --> 00:01:19.378
-First and foremost,
how special you are.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:20.780
-Yeah, right!
We'll cover that.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:24.583
But, also, I wanted to tell you
that you make me feel,

00:01:24.583 --> 00:01:31.657
you make me feel,
you make me feel...

00:01:31.657 --> 00:01:33.826
-Good.
-You make me feel good,

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:36.462
I guess is the point, right?
That's -- And I get --

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:38.297
Also, that I get
a little nervous sometimes.

00:01:38.297 --> 00:01:39.365
You make me a little nervous.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:44.670
-And I never met anyone
like you before.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.973
-I mean --
[ Clears throat ]

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:50.443
I mean, I've met
women before, of course.

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.612
I mean, I've met women who are
orthodontists like you are,

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:57.083
but -- but my current
orthodontist, she's a woman.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.252
-But you're the only one
in my mouth.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.720
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.988 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:06.125
You the only one that floats
down my root canal.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:08.127
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.164 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:13.699
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:13.699 --> 00:02:16.603
You talkin' about the girl
we're singing about?

00:02:16.603 --> 00:02:18.437
-Yeah, yeah, yeah!
Her! Oh, yes, yes, yes!

00:02:18.437 --> 00:02:20.573
-Oh, yeah, perfect.
No, of course.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.509
-This set has every Take Two
every song ever recorded.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:26.345
Well, maybe they're more just
intros than actual songs,

00:02:26.345 --> 00:02:28.180
but they're still smooth.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.884
Like their 1993 classic,
"Hey Girl, We Good?"

00:02:31.884 --> 00:02:35.621 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:35.621 --> 00:02:39.292
-Hey, girl, we good?

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:41.394
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:45.999
-♪ It's been a while
since you've been around ♪

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:51.871
-♪ And at night,
I've been missing you ♪

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.006
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.006 --> 00:02:56.175 line:0%
♪♪

00:02:56.175 --> 00:02:59.178
-It goes like this.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:03.016
I recently moved, so my mail
is still all messed up.

00:03:03.016 --> 00:03:04.817
So, you know how that goes.

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.919
You -- You got to get
a forwarding address.

00:03:06.919 --> 00:03:08.988
It's a whole thing.
-Yeah, and I've been getting --

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:13.826
I've been getting mail
from alumni Purdue.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:15.662
And I ain't even go to Purdue.

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:16.762
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.762 --> 00:03:18.030 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:18.030 --> 00:03:23.236
-Now, usually I just leave that
in the mailbox,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.638
let the postal worker
take it back.

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:28.474
You know, but some--
but sometimes it's --

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.978
Mm.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:35.280
-Ooh, sometimes...

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.184
-Sometimes I flip through them.

00:03:38.184 --> 00:03:40.553
♪ I-I just flip through them ♪

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.122
-Flip.
-I'm like a flip.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.791
-♪ Flip ♪

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:48.061
-♪ I got a little finger flip ♪

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.230
-♪ Why don't you flip? ♪

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:55.601
-♪ Finger flip through,
the Purdue University book ♪

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:57.670 line:0%
♪♪

00:03:57.670 --> 00:04:00.240
-I just saw that
Orville Redenbacher

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.208
used to go Purdue.
Did you know that?

00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:03.376
-Wait a minute.
That's the popcorn dude?

00:04:03.376 --> 00:04:04.911
-Yeah, that's the popcorn
with the bow tie.

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:05.912
-Neat.

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:07.747
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:11.184
-Like holiday songs?
How about holiday intros?

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.986
'Cause we've got all
of Take Two's seasonal hits,

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:17.189
including
"Hey Girl, It's Halloween."

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:18.691 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.125
-Don't worry, baby.

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:24.397
I will hold you close
when we watch a scary movie.

00:04:24.397 --> 00:04:27.600
-Oh, I like scary movies.
Do you, girl?

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:30.836
Well, uh -- huh?
-How about -- How about --

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:34.640
What movies are you discussing?
Really scary or...?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.844
-Any type of movie you want to
talk about, my vanilla friend.

00:04:38.844 --> 00:04:40.546 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:43.182
-How about scary movies
like "Jaws"?

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:46.718
-"Jaws," yes!
Well, "Jaws" isn't technically

00:04:46.718 --> 00:04:50.990
a scary movie, because that's
not really for Halloween.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:53.258
-Well, it is a scary movie.
If you watch it in October,

00:04:53.258 --> 00:04:54.627
I guess that makes it
a Halloween movie.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:57.497
-"Jaws" literally takes place
on the 4th of July.

00:04:57.497 --> 00:04:58.864
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:00.900
That is the complete opposite
of Halloween.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.704 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.905
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.905 --> 00:05:10.276
-I always --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:12.812
I always thought the opposite of
Halloween was Valentine's Day.

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:16.315
Sort of different ends
of the love-fear spectrum

00:05:16.315 --> 00:05:18.517
kind of, you know?
-Okay, I'll give you that.

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:20.386
But still, it's not Halloween.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:22.922
There's no line
in the "Monster Mash" like,

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:26.092
"Here comes Jaws, the shark."

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.526
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:29.562
-Pretty sure
his name is just Jaws,

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:32.097
Not Jaws, the shark.
-I swear to God.

00:05:32.097 --> 00:05:33.633
-Oh, no, man.

00:05:33.633 --> 00:05:35.901
-Plus, this set
is loaded with rare,

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:38.838
never-before-heard
Take Two jams.

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:41.073 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:41.073 --> 00:05:45.144
-Hey, girl.
It takes dos.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:48.447
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:52.285
-Oh!
Exhale.

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.720
That was our original name,
Exhale.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.191
-It takes two.
-And that's us.

00:05:59.191 --> 00:06:01.793
-Yep.
I was just trying to corner

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:04.997
the Latin market with "dos."
-Oh, I understood.

00:06:04.997 --> 00:06:07.666
I understood.
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:09.735
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.670 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:14.640
-Muy bien. Gracias.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.742
We certainly have not run...

00:06:16.742 --> 00:06:18.944 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:18.944 --> 00:06:23.216
...out of flirty R&amp;B intros...

00:06:23.216 --> 00:06:26.652
talk, or anything like that.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.121
If you're thinkin' --
Get it, get it, get it.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:33.258
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.258 --> 00:06:35.694
Hey, you know what
I was thinking?

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:39.431
-What?
-One, because we are Part Two...

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.233
-Yeah.
-...why don't we sing

00:06:41.233 --> 00:06:43.569
a little something for them?
What do you think?

00:06:43.569 --> 00:06:44.603
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:44.603 --> 00:06:47.573
Just this once.
-Just this once.

00:06:47.573 --> 00:06:50.142
And by "it" -- by "it,
do you mean singing?

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.411
-Yeah.
Correct.

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:55.380
Yes. Yes, let's give it
to 'em like --

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:56.849
give it to 'em like...

00:06:56.849 --> 00:07:01.720
♪ Ye-a-a-a-a-a-a-ah ♪
-[ High-pitched vocalizing ]

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.724
-♪ Ooh, baby ♪
-♪ A-a-a-a-a-a-a-ah ♪

00:07:04.724 --> 00:07:10.729
-♪ What, what, what, what ♪
-♪ Oooooooooohh ♪

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:16.168
♪ Oooh, oooh ooh ♪
-♪ Wednesday, Thurs, Tuesday ♪

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:20.339
♪ Wednesday, Thursday ♪

00:07:20.339 --> 00:07:26.279
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:26.279 --> 00:07:28.647
-Order now.

00:07:28.647 --> 00:07:30.449
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:07:30.449 --> 00:07:32.518
-Jaime Foxx, everybody.
Stick around.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:34.820
More with Jamie after the break.

00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:37.456
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:37.456 --> 00:07:42.128 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:42.128 --> 00:07:44.230
-Jimmy Fallon in this house!

00:07:44.230 --> 00:07:46.966 line:0%
